;; Staying put is priced too (jobs.lib.walk-risk/stay-estimate): a hurt body that cannot heal (hunger, no food) in a dark cave with hostiles that reach it where it stands walks away from them although the walk is over what the call's worth buys; it must not wait on go-to's :risky, and it is not :stranded (that needs a walk dearer than staying, pinned in go-to-risk-test).
;; A dark cave: a stone block x 10..60 with a 3-wide corridor, the body in the middle of it at 3 hp looking west, two zombies (no AI, so they only count as known hostiles) in the corridor 10 and 12 blocks behind it, the goal 25 blocks east (the walk leads away from the zombies, so go-to's hostile-near check does not hold it). The call's worth is finite: a goal worth arriving at whatever it costs (the default) takes any risk.
;; Should-succeed: the walk's risk is over the 2 hp the worth buys at 3 hp but staying costs more (the zombies reach the body here), so go-to walks and arrives. Should-fail: it waits :risky, stops :stranded, or does not arrive.
{:defaults
 {:tags [:survival :movement :go-to]
  :time :any
  :plot {:height 12 :length 64 :light :dark}
  :blocks [[:fill [10 -4 14] [60 8 18] "stone"]
           [:fill [11 3 15] [55 4 17] "air"]]
  :body {:at [30.5 3 16.5] :yaw 90 :settle-s 3 :effects [["hunger" 300 255]]}
  :limit-s 90}
 :cases
 [{:name "walk-over-the-allowance-goes-when-staying-costs-more"
   :act [[:summon "zombie" [20.5 3 16.5] "{NoAI:1b}"]
         [:summon "zombie" [18.5 3 16.5] "{NoAI:1b}"]
         [:rcon "damage $BODY 17 minecraft:generic"]
         [:wait-s 6]
         [:job (jobs.movement.go-to {:pos #at [55 3 16] :range 1 :worth 600})]]
   :expect [{:event {:source :job :kind :completed :data {:arrived true}} :within-s 40 :of-job true}
            {:no-event {:source :job :kind :waiting :data {:reason :risky}} :for-s 20 :until {:source :job :kind :completed} :of-job true}]}]}
